  "configuration_id": "config_038",
  "reason": "The current best (config_009, 0.725 acc) uses scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted. All multiprofile variants around this core have been explored (transformer/avgpool × weighted/concat), yielding a narrow 0.706–0.725 band. The singleprofile setting has not been tested at all, leaving an important design uncertainty: whether the aggregation step (transformer/avgpool) is genuinely adding signal or introducing noise that a direct weighted fusion of single-profile features could avoid. config_038 keeps the proven best RNA encoder (scvi_n200), best image encoder (imagenet_vit_l), and best fusion (weighted) while removing aggregation, directly testing this question. With only 2 experiments remaining, this is the highest-information choice: if singleprofile matches or exceeds 0.725, the remaining budget can exploit a new design axis; if it falls short, it confirms the current best and validates the multiprofile+aggregation architecture, allowing the final experiments to focus on fine-grained perturbations of the known optimum."
}

